{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Design review decisions (operator-approved 2026-08-02):\n\n1. ELIGIBILITY BROADENED: the contributor trigger must allow re-review of ANYTHING that is not an actual 'BLOCK — finding' verdict. That includes every coverage-gap sub-reason (llm-unavailable, review-error, scanner, indeterminate, gate-disabled) and the escalated -1 that 0347's bounded retry casts after exhausting attempts. Rationale: this is the manual escape hatch to retry once an otherwise non-retryable failure has been CORRECTED (credentials fixed, gate re-enabled, provider recovered) — so even 'gate-disabled', where an automatic retry is pointless, is contributor-retryable manually. The single hard refusal is a real finding: an LLM reviewer is stochastic, and unrestricted retry of a genuine BLOCK is 'roll the dice until +1' — this is why the eligibility line is stricter than Prow's /retest (deterministic CI can allow retrying real failures; a stochastic reviewer cannot).\n\n2. HARMONIZE WITH 0347 (lands first): after 0347, retryable failures mostly leave no vote and self-heal via the backfill reconciler; this ticket's remaining audience is the escalated/terminal -1. The trigger should therefore be implemented as 'reset 0347's per-revision retry budget and re-drive the review' on the SHARED retry-bound state, not a parallel retry mechanism. The spam/loop bound in the ACs is satisfied by that same shared budget.\n\n3. Design precedent confirmed: magic Gerrit comment in the spirit of recheck (Zuul recheck / Prow /retest / bors retry), eligibility decided privileged-side from durable state (the persisted code_review artifact discriminator, not vote-message text)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785695719100705001,"uuid":"ef230a17-4c2e-4216-a444-fd44e63300fd"}